      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's understandable that you want to continue supplementation, taking high doses of vitamin K while on warfarin can still interact with your medication and potentially cause bleeding issues, even if you're feeling fine now. Vitamin K can also reduce the effectiveness of warfarin, but this may not become apparent until your warfarin levels are checked at your next appointment. Continuing to take high doses of vitamin K without consulting your doctor may not be ideal, and it's better to wait until your appointment to get personalized guidance.",
